      "math_academy_id": "q-23089",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the function $y=(x-2)^{2}+2?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the graph of $y=(x-h)^{2}+k$ is a translation of the standard parabola $y={x}^{2}$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up.\n\nThe vertex of $y=(x-h)^{2}+k$ is located at $(h,k).$\n\nHere, the parabola is translated $2$ units *right*, so we have $h=2.$ The parabola is also translated $2$ units *up*, so we have $k=2.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218419/assets/4e43c68bd7ab2da6fb0be21ecc69ab29e111c442219caaae70b819e9df3488be.png)\n\nThe vertex is located at $(2,2),$ and these are the coordinates of the minimum point.",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
